meta {
  name: 40 List Grouped Samples (Grouping Settings)
  type: http
  seq: 40
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/accession/order-samples/grouped?page=1
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  page: 1
  ~status: NEW
  ~search: ACC-00001
  ~tatStatus: WITHIN
  ~dateFrom: 2026-07-01
  ~dateTo: 2026-07-31
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
  test("groups carry groupType + actionScope + sampleIds", function () {
    const d = res.getBody().data;
    if (d.length) {
      expect(d[0]).to.have.property("groupType");
      expect(d[0]).to.have.property("actionScope");
      expect(d[0]).to.have.property("sampleIds");
    }
  });
}

docs {
  Grouped, **group-paginated** in-house list (10 groups/page) — the same filters
  as `01 List Samples`, but records are grouped and the pagination unit is the
  group, per the tenant's Grouping Settings
  (`GET/PUT /tenant/accession-settings/grouping-mode`,
  `AccessionGroupingMode`). The in-house-orders page renders + scopes actions from
  this response.

  ## Grouping mode → response shape (set via Assessment Settings)

  - `SAMPLE_NAME` (Sample-wise) — `groupType: ORDER`, `actionScope: SAMPLE`
    (order header, each sample acted on individually).
  - `ORDER` (Order-wise) — `groupType: ORDER`, `actionScope: ORDER`
    (one action set for the whole order).
  - `DEPARTMENT` (Department-wise) — `groupType: DEPARTMENT`,
    `actionScope: DEPARTMENT` (one action set per department, across orders).
  - `DEPARTMENT_SAMPLE_NAME` (Department + Sample-wise) — `groupType: DEPARTMENT`,
    `actionScope: DEPARTMENT_SAMPLE`, with nested `subGroups[]` keyed by sample.

  ## Each group carries

  - `groupKey` — the order id or department id (null = "Unassigned" department).
  - `order` (ORDER groups) / `department: { id, name }` (DEPARTMENT groups) —
    header context.
  - `samples[]` — the group's list rows (each with `tatStatus` + `departmentName`).
  - `sampleIds[]` — the flat set a group action targets (sent to a `bulk/<action>`
    with `skipInvalid: true` — see the bulk action requests).
  - `subGroups[]` — only in `DEPARTMENT_SAMPLE_NAME` mode.

  `meta.total` / `meta.totalPages` count **groups**, not samples.
}
